Scoring formula b3.v7 (docs/proposals/scoring.md R1, R2, R4-R10)

The loop guard (scripts/loop_guard.py) keeps a session from editing pickfit/score.py, pickfit/schema.py and
schema/, so these changes are proposed here instead of committed. It applies on top of branch proposals/scoring
(after the R3, R8-tooling and R2-set commits) and also touches the unprotected files that only work with it: the
R4 part of pickfit/extract.py, pickfit/cli.py (score flags), pickfit/discover/store.py (ReadOnlyPipelineDB), the
recompute, backfill, priors and comparison scripts, and the tests.

    git apply --check loop/proposals/scoring-b3v7.patch
    git apply loop/proposals/scoring-b3v7.patch
    uv run pytest

What it does:
- R1: scores.inputs keeps the raw GitHub signals and issues; maintenance, hygiene and responsiveness are computed
  from them, refresh_scores recomputes every part with no call (R10); scripts/migrate_score_inputs.py backfills
  inputs from runs/pipeline.db.
- R2: DocsRubric keeps prompt_version, input_sha, renderer_version and grader; scripts/compare_rubric.py compares
  prompts on scripts/rubric_calibration_set.json (paid, plans only without --run).
- R3 for the rubric: reused while input_sha is the same; --regrade-before / --regrade-model grade again by name.
- R4: extract.RUBRIC_IN_EXTRACTION (off) lets the extraction call grade the rubric; scoring then uses it.
- R5: quality.raw_total; security.assessment.level replaces the 79 cap (exposed: no treasure, -10; blocked: no
  treasure; conditional: a note); records without an assessment keep the cap; a fix out 90+ days off maintenance.
- R6: missing or thin components pulled toward the category mean (QUALITY_PRIORS, scripts/calibrate_quality_priors.py).
- R7: sandbox_verification x depth (install 0.8, MCP handshake 0.9, function/service/inference 1.0).
- R8: "other" and the five subject categories use the pooled popularity refs "_all", not dev_cli's.
- R9: schema.UNCHECKED_CAN_BE_TREASURE (default True: today's rule).
- R10: formula b3.v7; earlier formulas' results kept in scores.history.

